hadiths[22]{hadithnumber,text}:
"28","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that he stated: We performed sajdah (prostration) with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, in Surah Inshiqaq."
"29","It is narrated from Hazrat Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Holy Prophet ﷺ said: ""If a person finds his goods in their original state with an insolvent (bankrupt) person, then he has a greater right to that property."
"30","Ibn Al-Madini narrated to us, he said, Sufyan narrated to us from Amr bin Dinar, from Hisham bin Yahya, from our master Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, who narrated from the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, a narration similar to the previous hadith."
"31","Ibn al-Madini narrated to us a hadith, he said, Sufyan narrated to us from Amr bin Dinar, from Yahya bin Saeed, from Abu Bakr bin Muhammad, from Umar bin Abdul Aziz, from Abu Bakr bin Abdur Rahman, from our master Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him), who narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) a narration similar to the previous hadith."
"32","Abu Musa Ansari narrated to us the hadith, he said, Anas bin Iyad narrated to us from Yahya bin Saeed, from Abu Bakr bin Muhammad, from Umar bin Abdul Aziz, from Abu Bakr bin Abdur Rahman, from our master Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, who narrated from the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, a narration similar to the previous hadith."
"33","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: If a man becomes insolvent and the creditor finds his property with him in its original form, then he has more right to that property than others."
"34","Ahmad bin Abdullah narrated to us, he said, Abdur Rahman bin Mahdi narrated to us from Malik, he from Yahya bin Saeed, he from Abu Bakr bin Muhammad, he from Abu Bakr bin Abdur Rahman, he from our master Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, who narrated from the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him. In this chain, Abu Bakr bin Muhammad did not mention Umar bin Abdul Aziz, may Allah have mercy on him, as an intermediary."
"35","Abu Tahir narrated to us, he said, Abdullah bin Wahb narrated to us, he said, Malik informed me from Yahya bin Saeed, from Abu Bakr bin Muhammad, from Umar bin Abdul Aziz, from our master Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), who narrated similar to the previous hadith."
"36","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that he narrated from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, who said: ""If a person becomes insolvent, and the creditor finds his goods with him in their original form, then he is more entitled to them than others."
"37","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him), the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a man becomes insolvent and the creditor finds his goods with him in their original form, then he has a greater right to them."
"38","Al-Hadrami narrated to us the hadith, he said, Sufyan narrated to us from Amr bin Dinar, from Hisham, from Yahya, from our master Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him), who narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) a narration similar to the previous hadith."
"39","Al-Hadrami narrated to us the hadith, he said, Sufyan narrated to us from Amr, from Yahya bin Saeed, from Abu Bakr, from Umar bin Abdul Aziz, from the Prophet (peace be upon him), who narrated similar to the previous hadith."
"40","Abu Musa Al-Ansari narrated to us the hadith, he said, Anas bin Iyad narrated to us from Yahya bin Saeed, from Abu Bakr bin Muhammad, from Umar bin Abdul Aziz, from Abu Bakr bin Abdur Rahman, from our master Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him), who narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) a narration similar to the previous hadith."
"41","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: If a man becomes insolvent, and the creditor finds his property with him in its original form, then he is more entitled to it than others."
"42","Ahmad bin Abdullah narrated to us a hadith, he said, Abdur Rahman bin Mahdi narrated to us from Malik bin Anas, he from Yahya bin Saeed, he from Abu Bakr bin Muhammad, he from Abu Bakr bin Abdur Rahman, he from our master Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him), he narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). And Abu Bakr bin Muhammad did not mention Umar bin Abdul Aziz as an intermediary."
"43","Abu Tahir narrated to us, he said, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said, Malik informed me from Yahya, he from Abu Bakr bin Muhammad, he from Umar bin Abdul Aziz, he from Abu Bakr bin Abdur Rahman, he from our master Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him), he narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) a narration similar to the previous hadith."
"44","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever finds his exact property in the possession of an insolvent person, he has more right to it than the other creditors."
"45","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Ammar Mosuli narrated to us a hadith, he said, Zaid bin Abu Zarqa narrated to us a hadith, he said: Sufyan (may Allah have mercy on him) was asked, a man bought goods and became insolvent and the goods are still with him, he has not paid its price, while some people have paid the price. Should the creditor take his goods? So he narrated a hadith from Yahya bin Saeed, from Abu Bakr bin Muhammad bin Amr bin Hazm, from Umar bin Abdul Aziz, from our master Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), he narrated: The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever bought goods, then became insolvent, and the creditor found his goods with the insolvent, then he is more entitled to it than others."
"46","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Huraira, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Whoever finds his goods with a bankrupt person, he has more right to them."
"47","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever finds his own goods intact with a bankrupt person, he has more right to them."
"48","Abdur Rahman bin Abdullah bin Abdul Hakam narrated to us a hadith, he said, my father narrated to us a hadith, he said, Bakr bin Mudhar narrated to us from Ibn al-Had, he from Abu Bakr bin Muhammad, he from Umar bin Abdul Aziz, he from Abu Bakr bin Abdur Rahman, he from Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him), who narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) a narration similar to the previous hadith."
"49","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him), who narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him): ""Indeed, Allah Almighty began this (reformation of religion and world) with Prophethood and mercy, then there will be Caliphate, then kingship, then monarchy, then coercive kingship, then there will be bounty and honor."
